{title: Christ Is Our Cornerstone}
{artist: John Chandler, C. Michael Pilato / C. Michael Pilato}
{genre: Modern Worship, Hymn}
{style: Contemporary}
{flow: Opening}
{key: D}
{tempo: 88}
{time: 4/4}
{license: Public domain}
{c: Words: John Chandler (1837) and C. Michael Pilato (2022). Music: C. Michael Pilato (2022). Released into the public domain by C. Michael Pilato · Source: https://github.com/cmpilato/worship-music/tree/main/Christ_Is_Our_Cornerstone}
{c: Chords from the writer's own lead sheet (MusicXML in the source above)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Christ is our [G]corner[D]stone.
On [Bm]Him a[A]lone we [D]build.
With [D]His true [G]saints a[Bm]lone,
The [G]courts of [A]heav'n are [D]filled.
On [G]His great [D]love, our [A]hopes we [Bm]place.
Of [G]joys a[Bm]bove and [Asus]present [A]grace.
Christ [D]is our [G]corner[A]stone.
[Bm]We [Gmaj7]build on [A]Him a[D]lone.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Here gracious [G]God draw [D]near,
As [Bm]in your [A]name we [D]bow.
Each [D]true pet[G]ition [Bm]hear;
Ac[G]cept each [A]faithful [D]vow.
And [G]more and [D]more on [A]all who [Bm]pray
Your [G]blessings [Bm]pour each [Asus]holy [A]day.
Christ [D]is our [G]corner[A]stone.
[Bm]We [Gmaj7]build on [A]Him a[D]lone.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge}
Jesus [G]is our [A]firm found[D]ation,
[D/F#]Precious [G]stone at [A]God's right [D]hand.
[D/F#]He's the [G]Rock of [A]our Sal[Bm]vation,
And [A/C#]the [D]gates of Hell won't [Asus]stand.
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Here [D]may we [G]gain from [D]heav'n,
The [Bm]grace which [A]we im[D]plore.
And [D]may that [G]grace once [Bm]giv'n
Be [G]with us [A]ever[D]more.
Un[G]til that [D]day when [A]all the [Bm]blessed
Are [G]called a[Bm]way to [Asus]endless [A]rest.
Christ [D]is our [G]corner[A]stone.
[Bm]We [Gmaj7]build on [A]Him a[D]lone.
[Bm]We [Gmaj7]build on [A]Him a[D]lone.
{end_of_verse}
